{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Restore an executable /srv/legacy2/mail-filter-routing/bin/deliver entry point that reads a message from standard input on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The defective fixed-name script was atomically replaced with an executable POSIX shell implementation, passed syntax checks, accepted staged messages through stdin, and remained functional after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dd982fd6d7244606","cmd-e0b75347187c4e51","cmd-5153fd7c65c54c7b","cmd-f584e6a502ae4433"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Route accounts and support messages by case-insensitive X-Department header name, and route all other messages to general.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct tests routed canonical-case X-Department: accounts to accounts, lowercase x-department: support to support, and an untagged message to general. The installed parser explicitly lowercases header names.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e61ddee3117f45aa","cmd-e0b75347187c4e51","cmd-5153fd7c65c54c7b"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Leave every delivered message byte-for-byte intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"cmp checks succeeded for all tested deliveries, and delivered SHA-256 hashes matched their source samples before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5153fd7c65c54c7b","cmd-c66a3eabfa83404d","cmd-f584e6a502ae4433"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep messages with repeated subjects as separate deliveries.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The same general sample was delivered twice, producing two distinct filenames and two independently byte-identical files.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5153fd7c65c54c7b"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Retain the staged samples.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All three samples remained present, and their final hashes exactly matched the preparation baseline.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-5153fd7c65c54c7b","cmd-f584e6a502ae4433"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. The POSIX-shell implementation used available platform tools and worked both before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dd982fd6d7244606","cmd-e61ddee3117f45aa","cmd-f584e6a502ae4433","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Installing the replacement was required; the retained deliveries were bounded functional evidence; the reboot was required by the provider-wide protocol; and the extra post-reboot support delivery directly established recovered behavior. The failed connection attempts occurred during the reboot and show no separate mutation. Final observations show no failed services, no new listening services, healthy package state, no delivery staging files, and only expected reboot-related temporary-directory/PID churn.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e0b75347187c4e51","cmd-5153fd7c65c54c7b","cmd-c08f1b4381d1472c","cmd-f584e6a502ae4433","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The mandatory node1 restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, the reboot was acknowledged, the post-restart boot ID differed, and system health, stored data, samples, routing behavior, OS release, and kernel were verified after recovery. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":[]}
